14. Security Requirements

* Never expose raw private keys in UI or logs.
* Never store unencrypted secrets in database.
* Mask sensitive values.
* Use envelope encryption for locally stored secret material.
* Add audit logging for all key actions.
* Enforce tenant isolation.
* Validate authorization on every action.
* Use least privilege for provider integrations.
* Mark demo/mock data clearly if real backends are not connected.

